configure-model-navigation-with-keybindings

Lane: frontend

Unit: control-model-and-reasoning-with-keyboard

ChildPatch: configure-model-navigation-with-keybindings

Form: GitDiff

Segment: snapshot

Purpose: Control the active model and reasoning effort through configurable session-local keyboard shortcuts and display reasoning strength in the TUI status line.

Requires: none

Provides: Previous and next model actions default to Alt-semicolon and Alt-apostrophe, follow visible picker order with wraparound, reset effort to the selected model default, and reject model changes during active turns. Reasoning shortcuts reach advertised Max and Ultra without persisting selections or opening a scope prompt. TUI reasoning uses six severity-colored cells with the red fast label immediately after them, matching live previews while terminal titles and other interface modes retain words.

Boundary: Own keymap configuration, runtime bindings and setup actions, shortcut dispatch, and reasoning status-line rendering. Preserve modal input, parent-owned input, reserve-model constraints, ordinary setting updates, native warnings and unrelated status items. Do not persist shortcut choices or alter provider/model discovery.

Verification: Focused configuration, keymap resolution, shortcut cycling and blocking, Plan scope, advanced reasoning, six-cell styling, fast-label order, terminal-title preservation, neighboring items and live preview tests.


